with each new episode of the white lotus  i find myself getting more invested in  what's going on with this group of  generally unlikable characters how's  this clash of the classes this group of  entitled guests and the staff that's  there to meet their every need how will  this all play out hey guys pete here  today i'm going to be talking about the  mystery of the dead body being loaded  onto the plane in the opening scene of  the white lotus there's just two  episodes left in the limited series and  this feels like a good time to talk  about how things might fall into place a  quick warning i'm making this video  after episode 4 which means there will  be spoilers if you aren't caught up to  that point with that out of the way  let's jump in the series opened with a  flash forward of shane alone at the  airport getting ready to board a flight  to honolulu deep in thought he's kind of  nervously playing with his wedding ring  and it looks like whatever he's thinking  about has him seething as two other  travelers ask him about his trip we  learned that he was there for his  honeymoon and stayed at the white lotus  when they hear that name they say they  heard someone was killed there and he  confirms that telling them the body is  being loaded onto their flight when they  ask where his wife is he gets tired of  talking in no uncertain terms he tells  them to leave him alone he gets up he  walks to the window where we see the  casket being loaded onto the plane  that's the setup his vacation's over and  he's upset his new wife isn't joining  him on this flight and someone got  killed at the resort where he was  staying at this point the show wants you  to think that it might have been his  wife who died but that seems less and  less likely as things progress in fact i  think his wife rachel is one of the  least likely of the possibilities and at  this point it feels a lot more like his  escalating battle with armon is gonna be  the reason she's not with him at the  airport and i guess i should make the  point that it could literally be any of  the guests at the resort someone getting  killed isn't to say someone was murdered  i think there's a good chance it could  be the result of an accident the  characters all have their flaws but none  of them seem like they would find  killing to be an easy thing to do plus  they all have their own internal stuff  going on in their own things to work out  which is really what the show's more  focused on it's not the kind of show  that's built on this central mystery  it's really rooted in these complex  characters and their affluence and  privilege provide fertile ground for  social commentary and satire i mentioned  the characters being generally unlikable  and it's impressive when you think about  how much care the writers took to keep  the scales tipped in that direction any  perceived redeeming quality is quickly  overshadowed and two-thirds of the way  through the season there are only a few  characters left who haven't revealed an  awful quality they all suck and it's  novel because you're bound to rank their  nastiness based on your own underlying  prejudices and grievances also in most  of the ongoing conflicts there's the  whole well he's not wrong kind of thing  going on for example shane is thoroughly  annoying but on the other side armin did  double book the honeymoon suite and he's  continued to lie to cover that up and  it's not doing any favors for anyone  while the casket mystery isn't the most  important thing going on in the show  it's still fun to speculate about who  might be in it so let's look at the  potential candidates except for armond  the staff are fairly undeveloped they're  there to support what feels like more  important developments in the plot with  the main cast and considering their  locals it doesn't seem like their bodies  would be flown anywhere if they were  killed i'll talk more about belinda in a  minute but up to this point she's been  one of the characters who doesn't appear  to have a dark side i don't think  killing kai or dylan would be that  impactful right now and overall don't  expect it to be one of them  kitty also seems pretty unlikely sure  she's annoying and she winds rachel up  you might be able to imagine a scenario  where things got out of hand and  something happened between those two but  shane looked angry he didn't look like  someone who was mourning the loss of a  loved one if it were rachel you would  expect that he'd be devastated they just  got married and from what we've seen  he'd probably be even more broken up if  it was his mother they seem to be very  close and he seems to take a lot of his  cues from her and yeah if you go back  and re-watch the scene he just doesn't  look like he's had that kind of loss  what's more likely is that he didn't  come out on top in the battle over the  room or he did and it was a pyrrhic  victory and in the process of getting  what he wanted in relation to armon he  took things too far he pissed off his  new bride and now he's traveling home  alone i also don't think there's a lot  pointing towards mark or nicole nicole  has the control thing going on and she's  great at injecting chaos into her  interactions with just about everyone  she takes a direct path to guide a  conversation and never fails to deliver  whatever it is that she wants to say  because of that i'd be pretty shocked if  she didn't survive in contrast mark has  been all over the place from the time  they arrived first he was sure he had  cancer then he found out about his dad  having sex with men and that information  put him on a bender since then armin has  been laying it on pretty heavy and been  pretty forward in their interactions but  things would have to go all kinds of  wrong for that to turn into him going  home in a coffin  something happening to one of their kids  seems a little more plausible olivia is  the kind of character who somewhat  performatively has a lot to say about  society and the shortcomings of her  parents she imagines herself to be  different than her family but there are  plenty of hints coming through her  relationship with paula that this might  not be the case  it's not unthinkable that she could get  involved in a situation that might put  her or someone nearby her in jeopardy  that could make for a dramatic situation  for quinn his age separates him from  being a fully formed unlikable character  he's a spoiled kid obsessed with his  electronics but he's a kid just the same  and after his gadgets all get washed  away into the ocean we see that he's  starting to open up to the world around  him  if we're thinking about the death being  an accident his diving lessons and  interest in the local boaters would put  him at a higher risk compared to the  rest of his family there's always an  impact when a young person dies and with  quinn appearing to be on a trajectory of  growth it would certainly make for a  memorable ending  the one new character is greg tanya  mistook him for a black lives matter  advocate his relative late entry into  the story makes it unclear if his death  would have much of an impact on anyone  but her there's always a chance that it  will turn out that that's exactly why  he's the one that gets killed but i  think it's too early to say  the last three characters are all  outsiders in a way and that makes them  seem like the most likely to die  paula's the friend that olivia was  allowed to bring with her and we've seen  that she has the idea that their friends  only so far as olivia knows that she has  more of everything because of that paul  has tried to keep her vacation fling  with kai a secret there appears to be  some history with olivia hooking up with  someone she was into in the past and now  we've seen that she's still being shady  there's a lot of potential for their  friendship not to make it out of the  vacation intact and as i said her  outsider status makes you wonder how  safe she is  armond is a character that's actively  spiraling and at this point he doesn't  seem capable of standing down in his  conflict with shane through his actions  he seems like the most likely candidate  to end up dead whether it be from an od  and his relapse or creating a situation  that would lead to a fatal accident it's  not immediately clear why they would  need to fly his body out if he died i  mean he's australian and of course they  could be shipping him back home to his  family but at the same time he's the  embodiment of the staff at the resort  this character has things down to a  science this is clear from his tropical  kabuki explanation to the trainee and  that centers his story around how things  turn out in his war with shane could it  end in death well we know shane won't  die he was the one that was in the flash  forward so armond is the only  possibility out of those two of course  their ongoing battle could just lead to  collateral damage and i think there's a  real possibility of that happening  that brings us to the last character and  the one i'm currently leaning towards  tanya maquad it's one syllable well two  syllables but the second part is one  syllable wad she stands out because  she's the only person traveling alone  and she's managed to put off almost all  of the other guests just by being  herself i mean she's carrying around her  mother's ashes and she hasn't been able  to let go of them and beyond just  looking for attention from a man which  is obvious in her interactions with greg  she appears to be completely rudderless  she's rich that affords her a  comfortable existence but she's an  absolute mess with belinda she's found  someone on the staff that she imagines  can solve her problems in her mind she's  able to connect in a way that she's not  able to with the other guests the people  from her class but she isn't able to  identify the power differential in how  her offer of financing a new business  affects things beyond it just being  something she wants to do she sees this  as a win-win situation and for us we can  see where belinda is coming from and  being reluctant to find hope in it  really happening that's what makes me  think tanya is the one who will die she  came alone and hasn't made any strong  connections with the mossbachers or the  patents and those people through the  lens of the story being a reflection of  the society we live in they exist in the  group that are pretty much always going  to be okay through their comments we get  the idea that mark and nicole fear a  loss of status and they worry about  their son's prospects in light of the  culture war but the reality is that  they're the ones who have the least to  worry about in the big picture on the  other hand belinda has something to lose  if things start to materialize with her  getting her own business and then tanya  were to die she would take that  opportunity with her and for now that's  what i'm guessing will happen at the end  of the series things might take a turn  in the last two episodes though i think  at its core we have a story about a  group of well-off people who see  themselves as having problems they do  have their own problems and so they run  off to hawaii to buy themselves some  relief the best resort the best scenery  and most importantly the best service  that money can buy the problem there is  the old saying that wherever you go you  take yourself with you and in the  scenario of the show they're coming  together and their intersections are  spreading those problems around i think  it should be fun to see how it all  resolves and i think that's a good place  to leave things in the comments let me  know who you think's in the casket and  how you hope to see the white lotus end  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon

